# The point at infinity of an elliptic curve is a rational place

For an elliptic Weierstrass curve `E` over a field `N`, the local ring of the point at infinity `O`
is the `N`-subalgebra `infPlace E ⊆ N(E)` generated by the chart-at-infinity coordinate ring
`infCoordRing E = N[1/x, y/x²]` and the inverses of its elements outside the maximal ideal
`infIdeal E = (1/x, y/x²)`.  This module records that `infPlace E` is a *rational place* of
`N(E)/N`: a discrete valuation ring with residue field `N` whose fraction field is `N(E)`.

The mathematical content is the team's `Work.MotC2.InfPlaceCore` chapter:

* `InfPlaceCore.instIsDiscreteValuationRing` : `↥(infPlace E)` is a discrete valuation ring — a
  Noetherian local domain which is not a field, with principal maximal ideal generated by
  `y/x²` (the chart relation `u·h = w·α`, with `h ≡ 1` modulo the maximal ideal, exhibits
  `u = w·α·h⁻¹`);
* `InfPlaceCore.residue_field` : the canonical map `N → ↥(infPlace E) ⧸ 𝔪` is bijective, since
  every element of the localization is a fraction `a/b` of chart-ring elements and, modulo `𝔪`,
  each of them is its constant term;
* `InfPlaceCore.frac_field` : every `f ∈ N(E)` is a quotient `s₁/s₂` of elements of `infPlace E`,
  because `x = (1/x)⁻¹` and `y = (y/x²)·x²` are quotients of elements of `infPlace E`, and the
  fraction field of `N[x,y] = N(E)` is therefore contained in that of `infPlace E`.

## Tags

elliptic curve, function field, place, discrete valuation ring, point at infinity
-/

import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.MotC2.Defs
import Submission.Work.MotC2.InfPlaceCore

set_option linter.unusedVariables false -- v435-speed

-- v435-port: begin
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false
-- v435-port: end

namespace Work.MotV

/-- The local ring `infPlace E` of the point at infinity of an elliptic Weierstrass curve `E` over
a field `N` is a rational place of the function field `N(E)/N`. -/
theorem infPlace_isRatPlace {N : Type*} [Field N] (E : WeierstrassCurve N) [E.IsElliptic] :
    Work.MotC2.IsRatPlace E (Work.MotC2.infPlace E) :=
  ⟨⟨Work.MotC2.InfPlaceCore.instIsDiscreteValuationRing E,
      Work.MotC2.InfPlaceCore.residue_field E⟩,
    Work.MotC2.InfPlaceCore.frac_field E⟩

end Work.MotV
